    <solution><p>Solution</p>
<p>The coordinates of a point are the pair <m>(x,y)</m> where <m>x</m> is the 
distance to the
right of the <m>y</m> axis (which is negative if the point is to the left of the
<m>y</m> axis) and <m>y</m> is the distance above the <m>x</m> axis.</p>
<p>The point <m>A</m> is 1 units to the right of the <m>y</m> axis and 4 units 
above the <m>x</m> axis
so its coordinates are (1,4).</p>
</solution>
